Pad every buffer the display gralloc allocates to a multiple of 16 rows (was 2).

Mesa's freedreno (the port's prebuilt Mesa 25.0.1, a6xx) resolves GMEM tiles to memory in 16x4 pixel blocks:
RB_BLIT_SCISSOR is rounded up and not clipped to the buffer. With 2-row padding, a buffer whose height is not
a multiple of 4 got GPU writes past its end. Seen on the OnePlus 6 (OH 7.0): a 759x1125 window was resolved as
768x1128 into a 1126-row buffer (crashdec of the GPU crash dump: RB_BLIT_SCISSOR_BR 767,1127, pitch 3072); the
IOMMU write fault was in the first page after the buffer. The overruns corrupt neighbouring GPU memory as well:
"CP illegal instruction", hang recovery, and twice a frozen phone. Apps with dialogs and other windows of odd
heights (Facebook, Xiaohongshu) and render_service's own off-screen buffers were hit. With 16-row padding the
same apps ran without one fault. The pitch is already a multiple of 32 pixels (msm dumb buffers), so the
16-pixel rounding across stays inside each row. The buffer handle keeps the requested width and height.

diff --git a/sdm845/hardware/display/src/display_gralloc/hi_gbm_internal.h b/sdm845/hardware/display/src/display_gralloc/hi_gbm_internal.h
index f7466b2..96d6b21 100755
--- a/sdm845/hardware/display/src/display_gralloc/hi_gbm_internal.h
+++ b/sdm845/hardware/display/src/display_gralloc/hi_gbm_internal.h
@@ -19,7 +19,11 @@
 namespace OHOS {
 namespace HDI {
 namespace DISPLAY {
-#define HEIGHT_ALIGN 2U
+/* Rows are padded to a multiple of 16. Mesa's freedreno (a6xx) resolves GMEM tiles in 16x4 pixel blocks
+ * (RB_BLIT_SCISSOR rounded up) without clipping them to the buffer: with only 2-row padding, a buffer whose
+ * height is not a multiple of 4 got GPU writes past its end (IOMMU write faults, and with them corrupted
+ * command streams: CP illegal instruction, hang recovery). The pitch is a multiple of 32 pixels already. */
+#define HEIGHT_ALIGN 16U
 #define WIDTH_ALIGN 8U
 
 #define MAX_PLANES 3
